# MIS SARL — Build a Gemini-Powered RFQ Import Assistant

Act as a senior Next.js engineer, TypeScript architect, Google Gemini API specialist, PostgreSQL developer, and business application architect.

You are working on the existing MIS SARL application.

## MAIN OBJECTIVE

Build a simple AI-powered workflow that allows MIS SARL users to import a customer's Request for Quotation (RFQ) as a PDF or image.

Gemini must extract the requested items, quantities, units, designations, and descriptions.

The application must then compare the extracted descriptions with the existing MIS SARL item catalogue.

The user must be able to review existing item matches and create missing catalogue items in bulk.

After validation, the application must automatically populate the existing quotation wizard with every imported line.

The user will then complete the customer selling prices and the remaining commercial information using the existing quotation workflow.

**This feature is intended to eliminate the manual process of searching and adding 40 or more quotation items individually.**

Do not build a second quotation system.

Do not build a new catalogue.

Reuse the current MIS SARL architecture and business logic.

