# PART 6 — MATCH EXTRACTED ITEMS AGAINST THE MIS CATALOGUE

After Gemini extraction succeeds, call a dedicated database matching service.

Suggested location:

`lib/db/rfq-item-matching.ts`

Or add the function to the existing item repository if that better matches the project architecture.

The matching query must compare only:

`items.designation`

`items.description`

Never query identifier tables or other item codes for this feature.

## Matching classifications

For every source line, return one of these statuses:

### MATCHED

A strong candidate exists in the existing catalogue.

Display the matched catalogue item and its designation.

Still require the user to confirm the selection.

### POSSIBLE_MATCH

One or more candidates exist, but the similarity is uncertain.

Display the best candidates with their descriptions and similarity scores.

The user must manually choose:

- Use an existing catalogue item.
- Create a new catalogue item instead.

### NEW

No convincing candidate exists.

Present the item as a new catalogue item to be created.

### NEEDS_REVIEW

Required extraction fields are incomplete or uncertain.

Allow the user to correct the designation, description, quantity or unit before continuing.

## Important matching behavior

Do not automatically create new catalogue items during the analysis phase.

Do not automatically associate an uncertain result with a catalogue item.

Do not merge separate RFQ lines just because their descriptions are similar.

Keep all source lines as separate quotation lines.

Use the source line number to preserve the original order.

Perform duplicate checks against the catalogue again immediately before creating a new item, because another user may have added the same description while the import review was open.

